## Appendix A
### Zig Build System Deep Dive

The Zig build system is not a configuration file parsed by a black-box tool; it is a declarative, executable Zig program that constructs a directed acyclic graph (DAG) of build steps. This appendix peels back every layer: from the simplest `zig build` invocation to custom build runners and multi-target cross-compilation matrices. By the end, you will see `build.zig` as a powerful metaprogram that can orchestrate any software pipeline—compilation, code generation, testing, packaging, and deployment—using pure Zig.

---

### 1. Basic Usage

A minimal `build.zig` looks like this:

```zig
const std = @import("std");

pub fn build(b: *std.Build) void {
    const target = b.standardTargetOptions(.{});
    const optimize = b.standardOptimizeOption(.{});

    const exe = b.addExecutable(.{
        .name = "myapp",
        .root_source_file = b.path("src/main.zig"),
        .target = target,
        .optimize = optimize,
    });

    b.installArtifact(exe);

    const run_cmd = b.addRunArtifact(exe);
    run_cmd.step.dependOn(b.getInstallStep());
    if (b.args) |args| {
        run_cmd.addArgs(args);
    }

    const run_step = b.step("run", "Run the app");
    run_step.dependOn(&run_cmd.step);
}
```

Key points:
- `b: *std.Build` is the entry point. It provides methods to create steps and targets.
- `b.standardTargetOptions(.{})` creates a target option that reads from `-Dtarget=` and defaults to the host.
- `b.standardOptimizeOption(.{})` reads `-Doptimize=` (Debug, ReleaseSafe, ReleaseFast, ReleaseSmall).
- `b.addExecutable(...)` returns a `*std.Build.Step.Compile`, which is a build step that compiles an executable.
- `b.installArtifact(exe)` creates an install step that copies the artifact to `zig-out/bin/`.
- `b.addRunArtifact(exe)` creates a step that runs the compiled executable.
- `b.step("run", "...")` declares a named top-level step accessible via `zig build run`.
- Steps form a DAG using `dependOn`.

A library is similar:

```zig
const lib = b.addStaticLibrary(.{
    .name = "mylib",
    .root_source_file = b.path("src/lib.zig"),
    .target = target,
    .optimize = optimize,
});
b.installArtifact(lib);
```

A test step:

```zig
const tests = b.addTest(.{
    .root_source_file = b.path("src/main.zig"),
    .target = target,
    .optimize = optimize,
});
const run_tests = b.addRunArtifact(tests);
const test_step = b.step("test", "Run unit tests");
test_step.dependOn(&run_tests.step);
```

